     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice that limit. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. I'd still recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
